Source: librknnrt
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-toolkit2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)

Package: librknnrt
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rockchip RKNN runtime for the NPU
 librknnrt is the userspace runtime for the Rockchip NPU: it loads an .rknn
 model and runs inference on the RKNPU cores through the kernel's RKNPU
 driver.
 .
 This package contains the runtime library. It has to be kept in step with
 the kernel's RKNPU driver, which it refuses to run against if too old.

Package: librknnrt-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: librknnrt (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rockchip RKNN runtime -- development headers
 This package contains rknn_api.h, rknn_matmul_api.h and rknn_custom_op.h,
 the headers for building against librknnrt. It is headers only: the .so
 symlink lives in librknnrt.

Package: rknn-server
Section: misc
Architecture: arm64
Depends: librknnrt (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rockchip RKNN debug server
 rknn_server runs on the board and lets rknn-toolkit2 on a host machine drive
 inference over a connection, which is how a model is checked against real
 hardware before it is deployed.
 .
 This package contains the server. It is separate from librknnrt so that
 installing the runtime does not start a daemon.
